    "description": "\"Man is involved in two freakish accidents that make him look like a murderer. Poverty row masterwork that is the most precise elucidation of the noir theme of explicit fatalism.\" - noir expert Spencer Selby |\n\nCast: Tom Neal, Ann Savage, Claudia Drake, Edmund MacDonald. | \nA B-movie, it was shot in six days. The film, budgeted for $89,000 and ended up costing $117,000 to make.",
